      "message": "One side effect of this that I notice in the site preview is that any object expansions that you do in the console tab are preserved when moving between tabs. I don\u0027t think this is necessarily a good or bad thing. Just a noticeable difference compared to the old system.\n\nI do wonder if this means that browsing through many log files will cause them all to sit in memory until the tab is closed? Testing this it does seem like log files may be slow on the first load but then quicker on subsequent loads. Trading memory for responsiveness is probably reasonable here. But something to keep in mind as some log files can be quite large. (and some of us have a really bad habit of not closing old zuul build tabs)",
      "revId": "b2f2192447f9753f08415f0b9c8bb36d2f4f0e5f",
