      "writtenOn": "2026-04-02T14:49:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While the state is now better preserved because this change isn\u0027t re-mounting components, the memory behavior is the same: the app has always stored all of the build outputs and all of the files in the redux store as long as the tab survives.  That can use a lot of memory, and I agree, we might not want to do it, and I\u0027m not sure I\u0027d implement it that way today.  But it\u0027s not a change.\n\nTo put it another way: there is a lot of memory use, but because of how we structured the redux store, not because of the react component states (which is what this change is focused on).\n\n* (I\u0027m not positive off the top of my head, but I think changing tenants may clear out the data structure we use.)",
